<%#
  The request could not be created. This was the 2021 design -- bg-red-200, a 150px inline SVG
  and a text-4xl heading -- and it was the last error UI in the app not on the design system.

  **The guidance sentence belongs to the caller.** Three forms render this partial, and only the
  caller knows what fields it has. The default describes item lines, which is right for
  `partners/requests` and `partners/individuals_requests`. `partners/family_requests` has no
  lines at all -- its only controls are a checkbox per child -- so it passes its own. Until it
  did, a partner who submitted with no children selected was told to check the item, quantity
  and pack unit on their lines, on a page that has none of those things.

  The `<ul>` below carries the specific errors either way; this sentence is the standing advice
  for the form, so it has to be true of the form.
%>
<%# `focusable` plus the controller is the same pairing `essentials_error_summary` uses: a failed
    submit re-renders the page with focus on <body>, so the partner starts at the top of a form that
    looks like the one they just sent. See `error_summary_controller`. %>
<%= render "shared/essentials/callout", tone: :danger, wrapper_class: "mb-6",
      focusable: true, data: {controller: "error-summary"},
      title: "That request could not be sent" do %>
  <p class="mt-1">
    <% if local_assigns[:guidance].present? %>
      <%= local_assigns[:guidance] %>
    <% else %>
      Every line needs an item selected and a quantity greater than zero.
      <% if Flipper.enabled?(:enable_packs) && (current_partner&.organization || current_organization).request_units.any? %>
        Items that come in packs also need a unit chosen.
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </p>
  <% if @errors.present? %>
    <ul class="mt-2 list-inside list-disc space-y-1">
      <% @errors.each do |error| %>
        <li><%= error.respond_to?(:message) ? error.message : error %></li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>
  <% end %>
  <% if current_partner %>
    <p class="mt-2">
      <%# Guarded on the address: mail_to with a blank email renders nothing, which left the
          sentence reading "Contact Some Bank at ." %>
      Still stuck? Contact <%= current_partner.organization.name %><% if current_partner.organization.email.present? %>
        at <%= mail_to current_partner.organization.email, class: "font-medium underline" %><% end %>.
    </p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
